# TLS material — all of it is generated by ./gen-cert.sh, and the CA private key
# is what makes the phone's trust meaningful. Committing the public halves is
# just as wrong: gen-cert.sh only regenerates the CA when device/ca.pem is
# absent, so a committed ca.pem makes a fresh clone skip CA generation and then
# fail signing the leaf against the ca.key it never had.
device/ca.key
device/ca.pem
device/ca.crt
device/cert.pem
device/cert.crt
device/key.pem
device/leaf.key
device/leaf.pem
device/*.srl
device/*.csr

# Build output + on-device state
device/bin/
device/token
device/**/httpd.log
*.log

# Local noise
.DS_Store
artifacts/

# Local config override (your device address) and its device-side copy.
config.local.env
device/config
